NAME = example_ethanol_single_point.inp
|  1> # ORCA input: energy and forces of one ethanol configuration at the level of theory of rMD17.
|  2> #
|  3> # Lines starting with # are comments. The line starting with ! holds the keywords:
|  4> #   PBE            exchange-correlation functional (a GGA), Perdew, Burke and Ernzerhof (1996)
|  5> #   def2-SVP       basis set, split valence with polarization functions (Weigend and Ahlrichs, 2005)
|  6> #   def2/J         auxiliary basis for the RI approximation of the Coulomb integrals (default for GGAs)
|  7> #   VeryTightSCF   SCF converged to 1e-9 Hartree, so that the forces carry no convergence noise
|  8> #   DefGrid3       the densest standard integration grid of ORCA 5 (rMD17 used Grid7 NoFinalGrid of ORCA 4)
|  9> #   EnGrad         compute the energy and its gradient; the gradient is written to <name>.engrad
| 10> #
| 11> # The geometry follows "* xyz charge multiplicity": neutral (0), closed shell (singlet, 1), positions in Å.
| 12> # This configuration is index 4823 of the rMD17 ethanol data (test set of split 1).
| 13> #
| 14> # Run:  bash orca/run_orca.sh orca/example_ethanol_single_point.inp     (about 5 s)
| 15> 
| 16> ! PBE def2-SVP def2/J VeryTightSCF DefGrid3 EnGrad
| 17> 
| 18> * xyz 0 1
| 19> C     -0.2864087200    -0.5292426500     0.0476115700
| 20> C     -0.9128728700     0.8836917900     0.2107592800
| 21> O      1.0729378200    -0.3867296100    -0.2003471200
